# What the serverless function does NOT need.
#
# The function answers /api, /auth and /healthz — JSON, from Postgres. Every
# byte here would otherwise be bundled into it and unpacked on every cold
# start, and `landing/` alone is 22 MB of fonts and images that the CDN serves
# directly and the function can never reach.
#
# This does not affect the static deploy: `npm run build:vercel` assembles
# dist/ from these directories, and dist/ is what ships to the CDN. Function
# bundling is driven by what the API entry file actually imports, not by
# what's present during the build — so keeping a directory available here
# doesn't put it in the function bundle unless the function imports from it.
#
# scripts/ and landing/ are deliberately NOT listed: build:vercel calls
# scripts/build-static.js directly, check:tokens/check:contrast/check:routes/
# check:vercel run from scripts/ too, and check:vercel scans landing/ for
# inline-script hashes to build the CSP — so Vercel needs both directories
# present during the build itself, even though the function never imports them.
#
# One consequence worth stating: with landing/ and public/ absent from the
# function bundle, `securityHeaders` finds no HTML and emits a CSP with no
# inline-script hashes. That is correct rather than a degradation — the
# function returns JSON, which has no inline scripts to permit. The HTML pages
# get their CSP from the headers block in vercel.json, which is generated from
# the same scan and gated by `npm run check:vercel`.

public/
legacy/
docs/
db/
.githooks/
.mirror-cache/

# Committed reference material and screenshots, not runtime code.
*.md
!README.md

# Test files never run in production and drag in their fixtures.
**/*.test.js
**/fixtures/
